'''thrum<sup>1</sup>''' (thrum), ''n.'' and ''a.'' [Early mod. E. also ''thrumb, thrumme''; < ME. ''thrum, thrumm'', a thrum (not found in AS.), = D. ''drom'' = OHG. MHG.

